#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/change-text-size-on-the-screen.md:0
msgid ""
"Make text larger in Ubuntu Desktop using Large Text, Tweaks or application "
"shortcuts if you have difficulty reading the screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/change-text-size-on-the-screen.md:7
msgid "Topics: Accessibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/change-text-size-on-the-screen.md:11
msgid "Change text size on the screen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/change-text-size-on-the-screen.md:13
msgid ""
"If you have difficulty reading the text on your screen, you can change the "
"size of the font."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/change-text-size-on-the-screen.md:15
msgid "Open the Activities overview and start typing **accessibility**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/change-text-size-on-the-screen.md:16
msgid "Click on {guilabel}`Accessibility` to open the panel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/change-text-size-on-the-screen.md:17
msgid "Open the {guilabel}`Seeing` section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/change-text-size-on-the-screen.md:18
msgid "Enable the {guilabel}`Large Text` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/change-text-size-on-the-screen.md:20
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can quickly change the text size by clicking the {ref}"
"`accessibility icon <find-the-accessibility-menu>` on the top bar and "
"selecting {guilabel}`Large Text`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/change-text-size-on-the-screen.md:22
msgid ""
"Large Text scales the text by 1.2 times. You can use Tweaks to make text "
"size bigger or smaller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/change-text-size-on-the-screen.md:25
msgid ""
"In many applications, you can increase the text size at any time by pressing "
"{kbd}`Ctrl++`. To reduce the text size, press {kbd}`Ctrl+-`."
msgstr ""
